*.csv
!fuel_analyst/supporting_data/plant_photoload.csv
!fuel_analyst/supporting_data/tree_parameters.csv

# Phase 4 committed C++-oracle golden dataset (scientific input/output CSVs
# only - manifests are .json and were never matched by the *.csv rule
# above). Narrow negation, not a blanket golden-tree exception: Phase 2's
# own goldens under test_golden_output/phase2/ stay force-tracked exactly
# as they already are (git add -f, see .gitattributes) and are
# deliberately NOT touched by this rule.
!tests/test_data/test_golden_output/phase4/**/*.csv

# Phase 5 committed C++-oracle golden dataset (soil_campbell scenario
# matrix). Same narrow negation as Phase 4's rule above, its own sibling
# tree - never merged with phase2/ or phase4/.
!tests/test_data/test_golden_output/phase5/**/*.csv

# Testing data (keep sample data in supporting_data only)
src/pyfofem/reference_docs/

